        "major_model_version": "v5.5",
        "model_name": "chirp-fenix",
        "metadata": {
          "tags": "Progressive neo-soul electronica, 7/8 time signature, 128 BPM, Steinway grand piano overtones, deep syncopated sub-bass, contrabass bassoon, weeping theremin lead, wide 3D binaural panning, organic groove, duets, smooth laid-back baritone male vocal, sultry enchanting alto female harmonies, hypnotic pitch-bending melody, zero intro, dynamic spatial contrast",
          "prompt": "Remixed from Open Melody \nhttps://suno.com/s/2LUgObG5NF9T9jeY\n\n———\nBlank canvas….\n\n———\nLet the noise fade to zero.\n\nIt’s not about the fear of where this goes, \nor the friction of the process.\n\nIt is about clarity.\n\nThe moment the hand touches the key, potential energy, flowing straight into the sound.\n\n\n———-\nA canvas left untouched is just silence in the dark...\n\nDon't let the time slip away.\n\n——-\nTurn the quiet into shape and form.\nUnshakable by the wind.\n\nThis music is for the listeners, \nthe poets, \nthe architects,\n\nfor those who know... \n\nand for those who are still searching.\n\nToday, we let the soul lead the hand.\n\n\n————\nEffortless flow is what we know!\n\nClear mind, clear heart, let it go.\n\nWatch the vision grow, \none step further today.\nEffortless flow is all we'll ever know…..\n\n———\nLa la tititi dum dom...\nTell me how much light can fit in our hand?\n\nLa la tititi dum dom...\nTell me how much light can fit in our hand?\n\nLa la tititi dum dom...\nTell me how much light can fit in our hand?\n\nStack it up... let it pass...\nReplayed... replayed.\n\n———-\nThey ask if we fit in a box not yet made,\nwith glass walls or a welded blade\n\nDo we belong beneath the dirt, unfound, unmarked?\n\nNo...\n\nWe don't belong to the ground at all.\n\nWe belong inside the sound.\n\nBecause:\n“What is inside was meant to be shared.”\n\n——\n86,400 seconds in a day...\nNo pressure. No fear.\n\nJust a quiet space to breathe before the melody returns.\n\n———-\nI don't need the power, \nI am grateful for the praise...\nJust the spirit moving through the keys we raise!\n\nNever mind the noise... listen to the Soul.\n\nTHE DISTANCE TRAVELED WHEN WE FINALLY HEAR IT!\n\n———\nEffortless flow is what we know!\nClear mind, clear heart...\n\nBring birth to the vision unknown.\n\nOne step further today.\n\nEffortless flow is all we'll ever know.\n\n——-\nFrom the hand, to the sky, \nfor all of us.\n\nYou are light... \n“Shine brighter at the darkest hour.”",
